  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LAC Regional (Honduras, Guatemala): Strengthening Anti-Corruption in the LAC Region                (SAC-LAC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To strengthen capacities of Honduran anti-corruption oversight mechanisms,                particularly in the Office of the Secretariat of Transparency and the Institute for Access to Public                Information. 2) To define and deliver targeted recommendations and related implementation tools to the                relevant institutions of Guatemala. 3) To improve networking and information-sharing among judicial                actors on anti-corruption in Honduras and Guatemala.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: (i) Honduras: The Office of the Secretary of Transparency,                and The Institute for Access to Public Information; and (ii) Guatemala: The Presidential Commission                Against Corruption in the Ministry of Interior.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to strengthen the legal and administrative framework to promote                greater transparency, accountability, and integrity in public institutions in the Latin America and                Caribbean (LAC) region.</narrative>
  </description>
